# Heartbeats — keep the lights on

Production is a single DigitalOcean droplet (`46.101.88.197`). When edge or SSH is unhealthy, **prioritize recovery** over new features.

## First action each heartbeat

1. Run `./scripts/heartbeat-stack.sh` or `./scripts/heartbeat-recover.sh` (~10s smoke + auto recover when SSH works).
2. If recover exits **2** (SSH down): **reboot the droplet in the DO console**, then `./scripts/wait-for-droplet.sh`.
3. If the disk line prints `WARN: root ≥88%`, run `./scripts/prune-droplet-docker.sh root@46.101.88.197` **in that same beat** — do not defer it to the next wedge. It takes ~25s and typically frees several GB (2026-08-15: 89% → 63%).
4. If the **cron snapshot** prints an `int <service>: FAIL` while edge is green, do not scroll past it. Green edge makes it look cosmetic, but `stack_health_last` uses the internal probes to pick a `diagnosis`, so a false FAIL sends the **next real outage** to the wrong recovery script. Fix the probe or the service in that beat. (2026-08-15: `int admin: FAIL (timeout)` for weeks — the probe was hitting the `force-dynamic` admin dashboard, which shells out to `docker ps`.)
5. On the VPS, periodic `droplet-ghcr-sync.sh` **skips image pulls** when root disk is **≥90%** (`SYNC_SKIP_IF_DISK_PCT_GE`) so sync does not re-wedge a full disk.
6. If `docker compose ps` shows apps with **`deploy_enabled=0`** still running (and they are not on the protected spine list), **stop them in that beat** (`scripts/stop-disabled-compose-apps.sh`). They fill `ACTIVATOR_MAX_CONCURRENT_APPS` so a host that actually had humans (anchor, zurichrunclubs) cannot cold-start. Periodic GHCR sync now runs that script; do not wait for the activator image. Bot-woken **enabled** extras (pocket, aiart, …) are stopped by `scripts/stop-nonessential-compose-apps.sh` (also on GHCR sync). Do not stop `anchor-api` or `zurichrunclubs` — they are `activator_never_evict`.
7. Read the **Evictable hot pool** line from `heartbeat-stack.sh`. `anchor-api` and `zurichrunclubs` are human-visited — do not stop them. Other names (pocket, tortellini, vc, …) are often bot-woken `deploy_enabled=1` apps. Do not start more apps that beat — they already fill LRU. Do not treat “lights on” as an empty droplet.
8. Read **Cold refs on always-on HTML**. The scan includes landing plus the homepage allowlist (anchor, zurichrunclubs, storybook, kidgift, 1pageresearch, maxlearn). Hits are leftover href/fetch/src to blog, agitweet, merch, marketing, or `github.com/216labs`. Then read **Cold refs in-repo** (`products/` `colabs/` `research/` — href and markdown, not hire-pin plaintext). Strip leftovers in that beat. Do not start those apps.

Do not spend the heartbeat on unrelated refactors while `admin.6cubed.app` and SSH are both down.

## Symptoms

| Signal | Likely cause |
|--------|----------------|
| SSH auth OK then "Timeout, server not responding" | Disk ~95% full or OOM; prune + reboot |
| `ssh: connection refused` during **image transfer** while edge still 200 | Piped `docker save \| ssh \| docker load` OOMed sshd, or `docker prune` on 1GB RAM. `deploy.sh` scp's a gzip tar at ~512 KB/s (`scp -l 4096`), waits again before `docker load -i`, keeps the local tar if transfer fails, and does a long SSH wait + one extra try. Retry; do not reboot solely for this. |
| cron-runner restart loop + SSH down, edge still 200 | Usually `SQLITE_CORRUPT` from changing `journal_mode` **on the host** while containers hold private WAL files. Reboot, then set DELETE **from inside** cron-runner/admin. Never `PRAGMA journal_mode=DELETE` from the host. |
| `edge-smoke` all `000` / unreachable | Caddy down or whole VPS wedged |
| `admin` 401 but other hosts timeout | Partial stack — run recover compose up |
| `int <svc>: FAIL` while ext is `OK (308)` | Usually the **probe**, not the service — internal probes must hit cheap endpoints (see `docs/STACK-HEALTH.md`) |
| `edge_proxy` / ext FAIL `ECONNREFUSED` `:80` while SSH OK | Caddy mid-recreate from GHCR sync. Recreate Caddy **only when the Caddyfile changed** (`scripts/lib/recreate-caddy-if-caddyfile-changed.sh`). |

## After lights are on

Distribution and paid work come next — see `heartbeat-monetization.mdc`. While human visitors are ~0, that means **sendable offers and outbound**, not Stripe keys or another app.
